.comment{
 GO HERE TO SEE THIS README AS A SLIDE SHOW!

    https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/readme-presentation/
}

.meta{
  title: "Slidedown - Text-first Presentation Compiler"
  css:
    ".container":
        font-size: "36px"
        line-height: "1.6"
}

.slide{
  .title{SLIDEDOWN}
  .body{
    .font-standard{SLIDEDOWN}

    Text-first presentation compiler with behavioral markup.\\

    .bf{View as Interactive Presentation:}\\
    https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/readme-presentation/\\

    .o{Documentation: docs/}
    .o{Examples: examples/}
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{What is slidedown?}
  .body{
    Do you like text? Have you ever wished that text was the\\
    basic substrate for compelling slideshows that are self\\
    contained and run in a browser?\\

    slidedown is a LaTeX-inspired markup language for creating\\
    interactive HTML presentations from plain text.

    .o{Text-first authoring - write presentations like you write code}
    .o{Behavioral markup - .directive\{content\} syntax}
    .o{Interactive effects - typewriter animations, progressive reveals}
    .o{Single-file workflow - one .sd source → standalone HTML}
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Themes}
  .body{
    Five built-in themes — each presentation below uses the same\\
    source compiled with a different theme:\\

    .o{.bf{conventional-light} → https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/themes/conventional-light/}
    .o{.bf{default} → https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/themes/default/}
    .o{.bf{lcars-lower-decks} → https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/themes/lcars-lower-decks/}
    .o{.bf{retro-terminal} → https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/themes/retro-terminal/}
    .o{.bf{terminal} → https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/themes/terminal/}

    Select with .tt{--theme <name>} at compile time.\\
    Runtime switching is not supported — each theme is a full compile.
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Quick Start}
  .body{
    .typewriter{> Installing slidedown...}

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
# Clone and set up
git clone https://github.com/FNNDSC/slidedown
cd slidedown
make dev

# Compile and serve a presentation
make presentation SOURCE=examples/minimal/minimal.sd

# Open http://localhost:8000
    }

    .bf{No make?} Use the .tt{slideshow} script directly:

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
./slideshow examples/minimal/minimal.sd --theme conventional-light
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Directive Syntax}
  .body{
    The core syntax is simple:

    .code{.syntax{language=text}
\.directive\{content\}
\.directive\{\.modifier\{value\} content\}
\.directive\{nested \.directives\{work\} too\}
    }

    .bf{Structure:}
    .o{\.slide\{\} - defines a slide}
    .o{\.title\{\} - slide title (metadata)}
    .o{\.body\{\} - slide content}

    .bf{Formatting:}
    .o{\.bf\{\} - bold}
    .o{\.em\{\} - italic}
    .o{\.tt\{\} - monospace}
    .o{\.code\{\} - code block}

    .bf{Effects:}
    .o{\.typewriter\{\} - typing animation}
    .o{\.o\{\} - progressive reveal bullets}
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Installation}
  .body{
    .bf{Recommended — via Makefile:}

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
git clone https://github.com/FNNDSC/slidedown
cd slidedown
make dev
    }

    .bf{Manual install:}

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -e ".[dev]"
    }

    .bf{Requirements:}
    .o{Python 3.11+}
    .o{pip or uv}
    .o{Modern web browser}

    .bf{Platforms:} Linux, macOS, Windows (WSL), Android (Termux)
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Usage}
  .body{
    .bf{Via Makefile:}

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
make presentation SOURCE=examples/minimal/minimal.sd
make presentation SOURCE=examples/minimal/minimal.sd THEME=retro-terminal PORT=9000
make compile SOURCE=examples/minimal/minimal.sd
make serve SOURCE=examples/minimal/minimal.sd
    }

    .bf{Via slideshow script:}

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
./slideshow path/to/deck.sd --theme lcars-lower-decks
./slideshow path/to/deck.sd --no-serve --outputdir /tmp/out
    }

    .bf{Direct CLI:}

    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
slidedown inputdir/ outputdir/ --inputFile deck.sd --theme terminal
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Example Presentation}
  .body{
    .font-standard{HELLO}

    Here's a minimal example:

    .code{.syntax{language=text}
\.slide\{
  \.title\{My First Slide\}
  \.body\{
    \.typewriter\{> Initializing presentation...\}

    \.bf\{Features:\}
    \.o\{\.em\{Text-first\} authoring\}
    \.o\{\.tt\{Behavioral\} markup\}
    \.o\{Interactive \.bf\{effects\}\}
  \}
\}
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Project Structure}
  .body{
    .code{.syntax{language=text}
slidedown/
├── src/
│   ├── __main__.py          # CLI entry point
│   ├── lib/
│   │   ├── parser.py        # .sd syntax parser
│   │   ├── lexer.py         # Tokenizer
│   │   ├── compiler.py      # AST → HTML compiler
│   │   ├── compiler_rendering.py
│   │   ├── compiler_assets.py
│   │   ├── directives.py    # Directive implementations
│   │   ├── theme.py         # Theme loader
│   │   └── theme_base.py    # Theme hook system
│   └── models/              # Type definitions
├── themes/                  # 5 built-in themes
├── assets/                  # CSS, JS, HTML templates
├── docs/                    # Documentation + hosted presentations
├── examples/                # Example .sd decks
└── tests/                   # 97 tests
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Testing}
  .body{
    .bf{Run all tests:}
    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
make test
    }

    .bf{Individual test files:}
    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
pytest tests/test_parser_basic.py -v
pytest tests/test_e2e_compilation.py -v
    }

    .bf{Coverage report:}
    .code{.syntax{language=bash}
make coverage
    }

    .bf{97 tests across 5 test files:}
    .o{test_parser_basic — directive parsing}
    .o{test_parser_modifiers — \.style\{\} and \.class\{\} extraction}
    .o{test_parser_nesting — recursive structure}
    .o{test_parser_escaping — escape sequences}
    .o{test_e2e_compilation — full pipeline integration}
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Architecture}
  .body{
    .bf{Functional Pipeline Pattern:}

    .code{.syntax{language=text}
.sd source → Parser → AST → Compiler → HTML
               ↓         ↓        ↓
          ProgramState → → → → → →
    }

    .bf{Key Concepts:}
    .o{.em{State Bus} - ProgramState dataclass carries state}
    .o{.em{Inside-Out Compilation} - children compiled first}
    .o{.em{Placeholder Substitution} - markers for child content}
    .o{.em{Theme Hook System} - themes subclass ThemeHooks for custom layouts}
    .o{.em{Directive Registry} - extensible handler system}
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{LCARS Theme}
  .body{
    The .bf{lcars-lower-decks} theme brings a Star Trek LCARS\\
    interface to your presentations.\\

    .bf{Dynamic scaling (v1.2.0):}
    .o{.tt{[} / .tt{]} — scale topbar up/down (100→75→50→25%)}
    .o{.tt{\{} / .tt{\}} — scale gutters up/down}
    .o{TB / GW on-screen buttons for touch/mouse}
    .o{Scale state persists across reloads via localStorage}

    .bf{Toggle chrome:}
    .o{HIDEDETAIL / SHOWDETAIL collapses the full topbar}
    .o{Smooth CSS transition animations}

    .bf{Live demo:}\\
    https://fnndsc.github.io/slidedown/themes/lcars-lower-decks/
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Development Status}
  .body{
    .bf{Working:}
    .o{Parser — recursive directive parsing}
    .o{Compiler — AST to HTML compilation}
    .o{CLI — functional command-line interface}
    .o{Tests — 97 tests passing}
    .o{Effects — typewriter, bullets, navigation}
    .o{Themes — 5 themes, extensible hook system}

    .bf{Features:}
    .o{Watermarks with percentage sizing}
    .o{Custom CSS via \.meta\{css: ...\}}
    .o{Navbar customization}
    .o{LCARS dynamic topbar/gutter scaling}
    .o{ASCII art (Figlet) and cowsay}
    .o{Per-slide density classes}
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{Contributing}
  .body{
    This project was developed with .em{test-driven development}:

    .o{Write tests first}
    .o{Implement to pass}
    .o{Refactor for clarity}
    .o{Document behavior}

    .bf{Code Style:}
    .o{RPN naming: .tt{object_verb}}
    .o{Type hints everywhere}
    .o{Docstrings with Args/Returns/Examples}
    .o{Functional over imperative}

    .bf{Get Involved:}
    .o{Report issues on GitHub}
    .o{Add new directive implementations}
    .o{Create example presentations}
    .o{Improve documentation}
  }
}

